From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jason Bruce Jones <jason@brucejones.biz>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 14:00:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/dp: equalize repeaters with TPS3 when TPS4 fails
 below HBR3

msm_dp_ctrl_link_train_2() picks the channel equalization pattern from
the sink's DPCD, so a sink that supports TPS4 gets TPS4 at every
LTTPR as well. Behind the PS8830 retimer on a Surface Laptop 7, the
retimer passes clock recovery but never reports CHANNEL_EQ_DONE with
TPS4 at HBR2: its PHY_REPEATER lane status reads 0x55 0x55 0x01 (clock
recovery, symbol lock and interlane alignment, no EQ done) and no
voltage swing or pre-emphasis change is requested. Every attempt at
every lane count fails and the monitor stays dark. Windows drives the
same retimer, cable and monitor (Dell U4919DW, 5120x1440@60, HBR2 x4).

TPS4 is only required at HBR3. When channel equalization at a repeater
fails with TPS4 at HBR2 or below, retry the training with TPS3 for the
repeaters before the existing fallbacks, which still apply if TPS3
fails too. The sink keeps TPS4. Links that train today never take this
path.

Tested on the Surface Laptop 7 15" (x1e80100-microsoft-romulus15)
with the Dell U4919DW over USB-C: the retimer equalizes with TPS3 on
the first attempt and the link comes up at HBR2 x4.

Assisted-by: Opus 5.5
Signed-off-by: Jason Bruce Jones <jason@brucejones.biz>
[Birk: keep TPS4 at the repeaters at HBR3. A lane count fallback restores
 the panel's highest rate, so the TPS3 override only applies at HBR2 and
 below.]
Signed-off-by: Birk Skyum <birk.skyum@pm.me>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_ctrl.c | 29 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 27 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_ctrl.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_ctrl.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_ctrl.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_ctrl.c
@@ -184,6 +184,11 @@ struct msm_dp_ctrl_private {
 	bool link_clks_on;
 	bool stream_clks_on;
 	bool sink_fec_ready;
+
+	/* Channel EQ at a repeater failed with TPS4 on the last attempt. */
+	bool lttpr_tps4_eq_failed;
+	/* Equalize repeaters with TPS3 instead of TPS4 for this link. */
+	bool lttpr_eq_tps3;
 };
 
 static inline u32 msm_dp_read_ahb(const struct msm_dp_ctrl_private *ctrl, u32 offset)
@@ -1820,8 +1825,11 @@ static int msm_dp_ctrl_link_train_2(stru
 	msm_dp_write_link(ctrl, REG_DP_STATE_CTRL, 0);
 
 	*training_step = DP_TRAINING_2;
+	ctrl->lttpr_tps4_eq_failed = false;
 
-	if (drm_dp_tps4_supported(panel->dpcd)) {
+	if (drm_dp_tps4_supported(panel->dpcd) &&
+	    !(ctrl->lttpr_eq_tps3 && dp_phy != DP_PHY_DPRX &&
+	      ctrl->link->link_params.rate <= 540000)) {
 		pattern = DP_TRAINING_PATTERN_4;
 		state_ctrl_bit = 4;
 	} else if (drm_dp_tps3_supported(panel->dpcd)) {
@@ -1857,6 +1865,8 @@ static int msm_dp_ctrl_link_train_2(stru
 
 	}
 
+	ctrl->lttpr_tps4_eq_failed = dp_phy != DP_PHY_DPRX && state_ctrl_bit == 4;
+
 	return -ETIMEDOUT;
 }
 
@@ -2944,6 +2954,8 @@ int msm_dp_ctrl_on_link(struct msm_dp_ct
 	if (rc)
 		return rc;
 
+	ctrl->lttpr_eq_tps3 = false;
+
 	while (--link_train_max_retries) {
 		training_step = DP_TRAINING_NONE;
 		rc = msm_dp_ctrl_setup_main_link(ctrl, panel, &training_step);
@@ -2983,7 +2995,20 @@ int msm_dp_ctrl_on_link(struct msm_dp_ct
 			if (!msm_dp_aux_link_plugged(ctrl->aux))
 				break;
 
-			if (!is_edp && same_params_retries-- > 0) {
+			if (ctrl->lttpr_tps4_eq_failed && !ctrl->lttpr_eq_tps3 &&
+			    ctrl->link->link_params.rate <= 540000 &&
+			    drm_dp_tps3_supported(panel->dpcd)) {
+				/*
+				 * TPS4 is only required at HBR3. Some repeaters
+				 * never report channel EQ done with it at lower
+				 * rates but equalize with TPS3, so retry with TPS3
+				 * before lowering the rate or the lane count.
+				 */
+				ctrl->lttpr_eq_tps3 = true;
+				link_train_max_retries++;
+				dev_info(ctrl->dev,
+					 "LTTPR channel EQ failed with TPS4, retrying with TPS3\n");
+			} else if (!is_edp && same_params_retries-- > 0) {
 				/* Retries at the same rate don't use up the fallback steps. */
 				link_train_max_retries++;
 				drm_dbg_dp(ctrl->drm_dev,
-- 
2.56.0
